  "id": "Compound::DB00665 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Nilutamide is shown to bind to Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolic pathways of diclofenac and arachidonic acid. This binding suggests a potential role for Nilutamide in modulating the activity of Cyp2c19, which in turn may influence the metabolism of its substrates. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Cyp2c8, a downstream participant of Cyp2c19, is involved in the metabolic processes of these substrates. The consistent binding of Nilutamide to Cyp2c19 and its involvement in the metabolic pathways of arachidonic acid and diclofenac suggest a mechanistic link between Nilutamide and Cyp2c8. The overlapping participation of Cyp2c8 in multiple metabolic pathways further supports the idea that Nilutamide may affect Cyp2c8 through its interaction with Cyp2c19. The integrated evidence highlights a plausible mechanism by which Nilutamide could influence Cyp2c8 activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
